# BluePrint3D — build-time config. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed VITE_. Restart the dev server after editing;
# these are baked in at build time, not read at runtime.

# ── Ask AI proxy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your deployed Cloudflare Worker (see proxy/README.md). When this is set, the
# app calls YOUR proxy, your Gemini key stays server-side, and USERS NEED NO KEY
# of their own — Ask shows "AI on" for everyone.
#
# LEAVE IT COMMENTED OUT until you have a real deployed URL. Any non-empty value
# makes the app treat the proxy as live: askBrain.answer() takes the proxy branch
# and NEVER falls back to the own-key path, so a placeholder here would break Ask
# for you right now and silently drop every question to the offline spec cards.
#
# VITE_ASK_PROXY_URL=https://ask-ai.<you>.workers.dev

# Dev-only: your Google AI Studio key, so the Ask AI panel stops asking for it
# on every origin (localhost vs the phone over the network are separate stores).
# DEV BUILDS ONLY — Vite inlines this at build time, so it is deliberately
# ignored in production builds; released apps still ask on the device.
# VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your-key-here
